{# Ward template: .github/copilot-instructions.md for operations/GitOps repositories #}
When reviewing changes in this GitOps operations repository, focus on the following areas:

## YAML & Helm
- Validate YAML syntax and indentation (2-space indent, no tabs)
- Check Helm `values.yaml` structure: all required fields present (image, resources, probes, service, ingress)
- Verify `Chart.yaml`: `appVersion` and chart `version` are set correctly
- Flag any hardcoded image tags that should use `latest` or semantic versions
- Ensure Helm template values are properly quoted when needed
- `tnn-app-generic` dependency version should use wildcard (`1.x.x`) for auto-resolution
- Verify `imagePullPolicy: Always` when using `latest` tags

## Secrets & Security
- No plaintext secrets, passwords, tokens, or credentials anywhere in the repo
- Secrets must use SealedSecrets (Bitnami) or Azure KeyVault references
- Flag any base64-encoded values that look like credentials but aren't SealedSecrets
- No sensitive data in ConfigMaps — use Secrets or KeyVault instead
- No wildcard RBAC permissions unless explicitly justified
- Azure Workload Identity: verify `azure.workload.identity/use: "true"` label is present on pods that need KeyVault access
- Service account must have the correct `azure.workload.identity/client-id` annotation

## Configuration Consistency
- Verify atest (`t-*`) and production (`p-*`) configs are structurally consistent
- Flag settings present in atest but missing in production (or vice versa)
- KeyVault endpoints must match environment: `t-{system-id}-{abbrev}` for atest, `p-{system-id}-{abbrev}` for prod
- Spring profiles: `spring.profiles.active=atest` in test, `spring.profiles.active=prod` in production
- No environment-specific values in base `application.yaml` — only in profile-specific files
- Verify no duplicate property keys within the same YAML file

## Resource & Probe Configuration
- Resource requests and limits must be set for all containers
- Production resource limits should be >= atest limits
- Liveness and readiness probes must be configured — prefer `/actuator/info` (not `/health`)
- `initialDelaySeconds` should be sufficient for Spring Boot startup (typically 60-90s)
- Verify `JAVA_TOOL_OPTIONS` includes reasonable `-Xms` and `-Xmx` values that fit within memory limits

## Deployment Safety
- Pod disruption budgets should exist for production services (`minAvailable: "1"`)
- Replica counts: production should have >= 2 replicas
- `telenor.no/auto-rollout-for-tags: latest` annotation must NOT be changed
